    "name": "Python program to find all those",
    "code": "# Python program to find all those\n# elements of arr1[] that are not\n# present in arr2[]\n \ndef relativeComplement(arr1, arr2, n, m):\n  \n    i = 0\n    j = 0\n    while (i < n and j < m):\n  \n        # If current element in arr2[] is\n        # greater, then arr1[i] can't be\n        # present in arr2[j..m-1]\n        if (arr1[i] < arr2[j]):\n            print(arr1[i] , \" \", end=\"\")\n            i += 1\n  \n            # Skipping smaller elements of\n            # arr2[]\n        elif (arr1[i] > arr2[j]):\n            j += 1\n  \n            # Equal elements found (skipping\n            # in both arrays)\n        elif (arr1[i] == arr2[j]):\n            i += 1\n            j += 1\n     \n    # Printing remaining elements of\n    # arr1[]\n    while (i < n):\n        print(arr1[i] , \" \", end=\"\")\n  \n# Driver code\narr1= [3, 6, 10, 12, 15]\narr2 = [1, 3, 5, 10, 16]\nn = len(arr1)\nm = len(arr2)\nrelativeComplement(arr1, arr2, n, m)\n \n# This code is contributed\n# by Anant Agarwal.",
